The architecture was informed by https://github.com/Herta-Network/libclash .
No runtime dependency on libclash or sing-box/experimental/libbox is used.

Host/control design was also informed by the user-provided desktop core
(module github.com/Ember-Moth/Solaris/src/core), including its protobuf
transport separation and host-owned Apple TUN descriptor lifecycle.
The pinned protoc archive metadata is adopted from that project's toolchain lock.

The shared Apple raw-FD host also follows the user-provided Hyper mobile and
HyperVPN desktop ownership model: NetworkExtension owns the original utun,
the embedded core owns a duplicate, and no packetFlow reader competes with it.

Additional Go dependencies retain their respective copyright and license
notices in their module sources. Versions and checksums are in go.mod/go.sum.
